 Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 315 PM MST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Numerous roads\nremain closed due to flooding.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 820 PM MST, - The stage at Durango was approaching the minor\nflood stage of 8 feet and the stage at Cedar Hill near the\nstateline was near major stage at 12.5 feet. - Forecast...the\nriver is expected to continue to fall below flood stage at\nDurango by late evening. This water will continue to work\ndownstream. The Cedar Hill gauge is forecast to drop below flood\nstage by late Tuesday afternoon. - Flood stage at Cedar Hill is\n10.5 feet.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nLightner Creek, Basin Creek and Animas River.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nAreas near Durango south to Bondad and the stateline.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-03T15:15:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.02f965ae74d4a09eb4bf05528d133991269cdbf9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.02f965ae74d4a09eb4bf05528d133991269cdbf9.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-03T05:33:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 030533 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1033 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Rivers across southwest CO and southeast UT remain high due to runoff. Several flood warnings will be in effect through Tuesday morning. - Tuesday will be dry with below normal temperatures. - A system is expected on Wednesday into Thursday morning. It wil","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-03T06:35:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume i